In this project I implemented the package trees using the class Tree
which works similarly to a facade by grouping together all of the
trunk, leaves, and fruit objects.
It both creates the objects as a unit and allows them to be
accessed together by the GameManager or Floral classes. (pretty functional oriented)

The trunk of the tree is just a normal Block for all intents and purposes
while the subclass Leaf extends Block and was created because I felt
Leaf has enough substance to justify a separate class (collision AND movement).
I considered trying a strategy design pattern but chose not to pursue due to
the complexity of needing to manage BOTH the collisions and movements through the
strategy and quite frankly, a lack of time.
Vaguely speaking I would probably use an interface with 2 functions to accomplish
the feat and then call the appropriate function from within Block's overriden functions.

Fruit was implemented as extending GameObject, but with a bit more time I probably could
have extended it from block or turned it into a strategy (the problem was that once set
the mass would cause bugs and I couldn't find the way to turn mass off in time to turn it in).

Finally the Flora class is in charge of the environment as a whole and so to some degree
works as a bigger encapsulating facade for when the entire environment must be managed or changed.